_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 110
---
order: 110
---
short_label: X.110
---
statement: If from a medial area there is subtracted a medial area incommensurable with the whole, then the two remaining irrational straight lines arise, either a second apotome of a medial straight line or a straight line which produce with a medial area a medial whole.
---
proof:

As in the foregoing figures, let there be subtracted the medial area *BD* incommensurable with the whole from the medial area *BC*.

I say that the side of *EC* is one of two irrational straight lines, either a second apotome of a medial straight line or a straight line which produces with a medial area a medial whole.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="280" height="240" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.110 diagram" src="propX110.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "X.110",
        elements: [
            "B0;point;free;30,-1000;0;0",
            "B3;point;free;30,1000;0;0",
            "A;point;lineSlider;B0,B3,0,190",
            "B;point;lineSlider;B0,B3,0,70",
            "C';point;perpendicular;A,B;0;0;0",
            "C;point;lineSlider;A,C',130,0",
            "BC;polygon;parallelogram;B,A,C;0;0;black;150,100,100",
            "D;point;lineSlider;A,C,90,0",
            "E;point;parallelogram;B,A,D",
            "BD;polygon;parallelogram;B,A,D;0;0;black;190,100,100",
            "F0;point;free;-1000,30;0;0",
            "F3;point;free;1000,30;0;0",
            "F;point;lineSlider;F0,F3,170,0",
            "G';point;perpendicular;F,F3;0;0",
            "G;point;lineSlider;F,G',0,210",
            "H;point;proportion;F,G,A,C,B,A,F,F3",
            "GH;polygon;parallelogram;G,F,H;0;0;black;150,100,100",
            "K;point;proportion;F,G,A,D,B,A,F,F3",
            "L;point;parallelogram;G,F,K",
            "GFKL;polygon;quadrilateral;G,F,K,L;0;0;black;190,100,100"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Since each of the rectangles *BC* and *BD* is medial, and *BC* is incommensurable with *BD*, therefore each of the straight lines *FH* and *FK* is rational and incommensurable in length with *FG*. [!just X.22]

Since *BC* is incommensurable with *BD*, that is, *GH* with *GK*, therefore *HF* is also incommensurable with *FK*. [!just VI.1, X.11]

Therefore *FH* and *FK* are rational straight lines commensurable in square only. Therefore *KH* is an apotome. [!just X.73]

If then the square on *FH* is greater than the square on *FK* by the square on a straight line commensurable with *FH*, while neither of the straight lines *FH* nor *FK* is commensurable in length with the rational straight line *FG* set out, then *KH* is a third apotome. [!just X.Def.III.3]

But *KL* is rational, and the rectangle contained by a rational straight line and a third apotome is irrational, and the side of it is irrational, and is called a second apotome of a medial straight line, so that the side of *LH*, that is, of *EC*, is a second apotome of a medial straight line. [!just X.93]

But, if the square on *FH* is greater than the square on *FK* by the square on a straight line incommensurable with *FH*, while neither of the straight lines *HF* nor *FK* is commensurable in length with *FG*, then *KH* is a sixth apotome. [!just X.Def.III.6]

But the side of the rectangle contained by a rational straight line and a sixth apotome is a straight line which produces with a medial area a medial whole. [!just X.96]

Therefore the side of *LH*, that is, of *EC*, is a straight line which produces with a medial area a medial whole.

Therefore, *if a medial area incommensurable with the whole is subtracted from a medial area, then two remaining irrational straight lines arise, either a second apotome of a medial straight line or a straight line which produces with a medial area a medial whole.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
---
body:

This proposition is not used in the rest of the *Elements*.
